LICENSING
=========

This repository contains code under two different licences. This file states
which applies where. Read it before copying anything out of this repository.

Previously this file contained the MIT licence text with no statement of scope,
which would have granted MIT rights over the entire repository — including the
proprietary parts listed below. That was not the intent.


1. MIT-LICENSED PARTS
---------------------

The following directories, and only these, are licensed under the MIT licence
reproduced in section 3:

    packages/cli
    packages/core
    packages/eval
    packages/schemas

Each of those directories also carries its own copy of the MIT text, so the
licence travels with the code when a package is published or vendored.

These are the open core. They are intended to be usable on their own, without
any of the proprietary parts.


2. PROPRIETARY PARTS
--------------------

All other content in this repository is proprietary and is NOT covered by the
MIT licence. This includes, without limitation:

    packages/pricing
    packages/ui
    apps/api
    apps/site
    apps/web
    services/github-app

